--- 4. create a 1 TB file (sparse) ---
    A sparse file has a real size in the inode but no allocated extents
    for the holes. This proves the filesystem can ADDRESS 1 TB; it does
    not prove 1 TB of data was written, and is not presented as if it did.

    apparent size (st_size)      : 1099511627776 bytes
    allocated blocks (st_blocks) : 0 x 512 bytes
      -rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1.0T Aug 26 03:14 /mnt/xfs/one-terabyte.img
      apparent: 1.0T	/mnt/xfs/one-terabyte.img
      on disk : 0	/mnt/xfs/one-terabyte.img
[PASS] a single file of exactly 1 TiB (1099511627776 bytes) exists on the filesystem
[PASS] it is genuinely sparse (0 blocks allocated) - honest about what this proves

--- 5. fallocate: reserve REAL extents, not holes ---
    This exercises the allocator itself. Sized to fit the 2 GiB image,
    because reserving 1 TB of real extents needs 1 TB of real space.
[PASS] fallocate reserved 1 GiB of real extents
    allocated blocks: 2097152 x 512 = 1073741824 bytes
[PASS] extents are really allocated, not sparse

    extent layout (XFS is extent-based, so 1 GiB is a handful of records,
    not 262144 individual block pointers):
      /mnt/xfs/real-extents.img:
       EXT: FILE-OFFSET         BLOCK-RANGE      AG AG-OFFSET          TOTAL
         0: [0..1041151]:       1048656..2089807  1 (80..1041231)    1041152
         1: [1041152..2082303]: 3145808..4186959  3 (80..1041231)    1041152
         2: [2082304..2097151]: 192..15039        0 (192..15039)       14848
      extent records for 1 GiB: 4

--- 6. allocation groups: XFS's parallelism unit ---
    agcount = 4
    Each allocation group has its own free-space and inode B+trees, and
    can be allocated from independently. That is why XFS scales with
    parallel writers where ext4's single block-group bitmap serialises.

--- 7. online growth ---
    XFS grows online and CANNOT be shrunk - a real trade-off, not a bug.
      loop now exposes 4.0 GiB
      data blocks changed from 524288 to 1048576
    size before growfs: 2.0G
    size after  growfs: 4.0G

